WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.260
- Lucky number seven is one that I know

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.530
I'm going to get heat for.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.840
Please don't attack me.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.410
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.960
I've watched a lot of medical dramas

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.240
over the last two years.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.540
Some of them really good,

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.330
and some of them that need
a little bit of improvement.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.623
A little bit.

00:00:17.623 --> 00:00:18.456
And to cap off the year,

00:00:18.456 --> 00:00:21.250
I'm gonna be ranking them
from least to most accurate.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.460
If you disagree with me on
any of these on the list

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.740
drop it down below in the comments.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.050
I want to know your thoughts.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.463
Let's get started. Boop!

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:31.450
Number 16, the least
accurate medical drama

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.470
that I watched on this
channel is "Attaway General".

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.080
Sorry to my Dixie D'Amelio fans out there.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.280
but the show just has inaccuracies galore.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.850
The uniforms aren't right.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.870
They're wearing hair nets at times.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.080
They're having teenagers deliver
medical care as volunteers.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.030
I literally remember
one scene when they were

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.540
trying to save someone's
life where the doctor was

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.040
like checking a pulse like this

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.730
and the EKG monitor just
has colorful strips going

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.620
across it, they mean absolutely nothing.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.130
Just nothing makes sense on the show.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.750
I get that it's young folks,

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.620
they're trying their first time at acting

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.770
and I support that, more power to them.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.800
I'm strictly talking about
the medical accuracy.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.767
Number 15, and the second
least accurate medical drama,

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:13.680
"Doogie Howser".

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.610
I can't believe it's this low on the list

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.100
but the reality is it's an older show,

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.880
so the medical accuracy is just not

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.400
up to par to our current standards.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.430
Also, I really remember
this one very awkward scene.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.534
- Doogie monster.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:28.900
- Whoa!

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.840
Maybe that kind of stuff
was okay back then,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.420
now it definitely freaked me out.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.280
Number 14, "Nurses".

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.680
I watched it with my
good friend Nurse Bianca,

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.900
who also was heavy critical of the show.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.510
There's just a lot of inaccuracies.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.040
They don't follow a lot
of the medical guidelines.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.650
Literally on the episode, they had one

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.160
of the nurses attacking another nurse

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.580
for treating someone
who is a known criminal.

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.390
We treat everybody in the medical space,

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:54.330
so that made no sense.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.480
And then in another scene
they had a doctor just say,

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.060
oh, we ran out of O blood,

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.690
so I'm just going to connect
myself cause I'm O blood

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:01.820
and give it to the patient.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.040
Like, no, sir, we don't do that.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.140
That is highly inaccurate.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.270
I'm calling BS.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.410
I love nurses, they're
the backbone of medicine.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.370
The show itself didn't do them justice.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.590
Lucky 13 is "Transplant".

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.270
I really liked the premise of this one.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.660
We have a Syrian refugee

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.530
that's thrust back into
practicing medicine in Canada.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.320
I was really excited for it to work.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:22.900
However, in the very first
scene you have an individual

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.080
who's not a doctor in Canada drilling

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.410
into someone's head in
order to save their life.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.900
Throughout the entire episode

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.500
no one was doing chest compressions.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.333
They were talking

00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:33.440
about intubating people,
getting cardiac consult.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.090
Where were the chest compressions?

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.720
Chest compressions, chest compressions,

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.170
chest compressions, folks.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.250
For number 12, we have "Royal Pains".

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.170
The medical accuracy is
just out of this world.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.380
It's almost like they're functioning

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.150
like an ER specialist,
family medicine doctor,

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.360
interventional cardiologist, toxicologist.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.760
It's like they're super human.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.150
He didn't even look at her eyes.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.840
How does he know what
her pupils look like?

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.480
It sounds like he has x-ray vision.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.880
He could see from across the room.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.340
That is not how a medical
diagnosis is made,

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.480
and I feel like it misguides people

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.630
into thinking doctors
have to know right away

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:05.463
what's going on.

00:03:05.463 --> 00:03:08.130
A lot of times we don't and we
have to investigate further.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.230
By the way, all the medical
dramas I'm ranking now

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.410
and I've reviewed in the
past are linked down below,

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.530
so if you want to watch one
of those in more detail,

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:15.363
check it out.

00:03:15.363 --> 00:03:17.760
Number 11, we have "The Night Shift".

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.700
I know that there's a lot of fans

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.370
on this show and they
may be upset seeing their

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.200
favorite medical drama
this low on the list.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.350
It's just not so medically accurate.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.170
At least to be fair, the
one episode I watched

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:33.443
they had one doctor
completely lose his mind.

00:03:33.443 --> 00:03:35.930
(people snarling)

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.620
Like there was just so much
unrealistic actions happening

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.210
by the staff that it made it
feel not medically accurate.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:44.110
Again, the procedures they showed,

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.400
the medical illnesses
they showed were so far

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.240
out there that you probably
wouldn't even find them

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.140
in a medical book.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.950
It would have to be a sub
subspecialist medical book

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.410
in order to find these conditions.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:56.040
Number 10, falling somewhere
in the middle of the list,

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.480
is "Nurse Jackie".

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.240
Now this show is darker

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.200
than most medical dramas on this list,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.900
and I actually really enjoyed
the depth of the show.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.499
However, the characters
were just so aggressive

00:04:07.499 --> 00:04:09.270
in their illegal action.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.900
If she forged his organ donor certificate

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.090
on the back of his license, that's crazy.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.290
Like there's just so many
things that keep happening to

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.760
make it seem outrageous,
to make it interesting,

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.000
it doesn't feel quite realistic.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.680
Coming in at number nine, "The Resident".

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.080
I actually got invited

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.670
by one of the cast members to be

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.000
on the set with them, got
a behind the scenes tour.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:29.910
Super cool.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.240
All that's linked down below.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.500
I think this show falls somewhere
in the middle of the pack

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.920
when it comes to medical accuracy.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.410
They use a lot of good medical
terms that are accurate.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.040
Their procedures are performed

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.730
with a decent level of accuracy.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.800
The one thing that I
will say is the residents

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.010
on the show are really
like cowboy residents.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.450
They're doing whatever they want.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:51.210
- You do whatever the hell I
tell you, no questions asked.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.940
- So that really isn't realistic,

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.910
and just like any good medical drama,

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:57.200
the drama's turned up all time high.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.430
While I dig the drama, the realism falls

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.750
somewhere right down the middle.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:01.890
Definitely one I enjoy though,

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:03.260
and I recommend you check it out as well.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.670
Number eight, we have "New Amsterdam".

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.270
All in all, I think it's a good show.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.550
It's quality, it talks
about really important

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.540
systemic issues within healthcare.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.490
While I think it takes
on important challenges,

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:16.480
it also does it in a very
unrealistic way at times.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.570
- Will everyone in the
cardiac surgical department

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.183
please raise your hands.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.280
Great, thank you. You're all fired.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.590
Like that is not realistic.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.740
Who's going to take care of
the patients in the meantime?

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.090
I definitely want to check
more episodes out of that show.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.100
If you have a specific
episode of "New Amsterdam"

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.520
you want me to watch, drop it down below.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.420
Lucky number seven is one that I know

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.700
I'm going to get heat for.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:37.990
Please don't attack me.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:41.140
I'm sorry, I'm sorry,
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:45.090
I'm saying it now, I'm
sorry. "Grey's Anatomy".

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.120
I know, I know it's so, it's, it's not,

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.610
it's not that accurate.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.220
I know it's the most popular medical drama

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.850
of all time probably.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.930
And look, I've watched four
episodes of it on this channel.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.290
I've probably watched maybe
a handful more on my own

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.450
and it's just not medically accurate.

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.630
Residents and interns are doing all sorts

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.060
of advanced procedures with no oversight,

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:09.230
romance around every corner
and heartbreak and drama,

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:10.850
and I know why so many of you love it.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.004
I get it. I like it too, it's...

00:06:13.004 --> 00:06:13.837
(loud smooching)

00:06:13.837 --> 00:06:16.600
But still, medical accuracy,
just, it's not there.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.640
For number six, we have "Scrubs".

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:22.710
Yes, the famous, famous
satirical medical show "Scrubs".

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.520
I honestly struggled with this one.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.760
I didn't know where to place it.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.130
I know many of you at home, on forums,

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.170
say "Scrubs" is the most accurate show.

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.420
However, I do think that it is an accurate

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.610
satirical explanation of what happens,

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:38.910
or representation of what
happens in hospitals,

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.190
but it is not medically accurate.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:42.380
- Get her to open her mouth,

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.520
take a handful and throw it at her.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.767
Whatever sticks, that's
the correct dosage.

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:49.440
- And it's a comedy, so I
get why they're doing it

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.870
and I enjoy watching it,
but one of the things

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.300
that kind of irks me with the show

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.270
maybe because I'm so
defensive and protective

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.090
of my patients is I feel like they're mean

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.300
to their patients sometimes.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:06:59.180
And I know it's a joke

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.600
but somehow it just gets in here for me.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.440
Number five, we have "Chicago Med".

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.700
A lot of these shows really
just focus on doctors

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:08.490
and "Chicago Med" really does a great job

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.830
at showing nurses as
part of the medical team.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.040
The episode that I watched

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.800
I couldn't find almost anything
medically wrong with it.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.460
It has good medical terminology,

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.260
the procedures that
they're doing are accurate,

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:19.900
and the fact that they had a nurse

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:22.670
telling a resident how to do
chest compressions properly,

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:23.800
they were critiquing them,

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:24.910
that got me hyped.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.210
Number four, we have "Code Black".

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.740
This is the surprising one on the list.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.580
The dark horse, the
black sheep, if you will.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:35.090
I really fell in love with this show.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:38.070
It actually genuinely upset me
to find out it was canceled.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:40.620
The show felt like it was
written by medical professionals,

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.380
and then someone added a little drama,

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:44.810
as opposed to someone
that writes medical dramas

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.690
and then they sprinkled
some medicine into it.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:48.950
I think that the real hard hitting truth

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.100
about the show is it does a good job

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:55.010
at showing character development
of medical professionals.

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.090
The stresses we have,
the struggles we have,

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:00.010
how we go about losing patients
and talking with patients.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:03.280
I think those were very
real and clearly scripted

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.160
by someone who's gone
through that process.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:05.993
Let's bring it back.

00:08:05.993 --> 00:08:07.960
Let's resurrect "Code
Black". Who's with me?

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.380
Number three, we have "House MD".

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.240
I know so many House fans
wanted him to be number one,

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.490
and while the show has
incredible scientific rigor,

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.300
like it talks about true
scientific conditions,

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.370
a lot of the zebra
conditions that we've talked

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:24.230
about on this channel, ones
that warrant more attention.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.680
And while I think that's great,

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.290
I think the way that my
man House MD goes about it

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.650
is just reckless.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.520
- I want to check for Erdheim-Chester.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:32.650
- How does he know what that is?

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:33.610
I've never even heard of it.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.430
He's funny, he's interesting, he's wacky.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.860
He argues with people,
but also the residents

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.240
and the fellows that are with him,

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.520
they each bring their own
unique spin on the show.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:43.610
So I'm a huge fan.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:45.770
I want to watch more
episodes of "House MD"

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:47.240
and I have it third on my list.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:48.930
I wonder where it falls on yours.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:52.470
We're at the top two folks,
it's getting serious.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.330
The competition is heating up.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:57.430
Number two is "The Good Doctor".

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:00.840
Dr. Shaun comes in with the accuracy.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:04.300
The big thing, a true medical
professional, who is diagnosed

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:07.180
with autism, but is still
doing their job phenomenally.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.240
When they talk about medical conditions,

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:11.150
the way that they talk about it

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.200
in a reasonable, easy to understand way,

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.910
but still using medical
terminology is awesome.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.440
I love that they manage to inject humor

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.793
even some of the most dark spots.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.610
- Do you need me to listen to you anymore?

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:25.443
- No, Shaun.

00:09:25.443 --> 00:09:26.760
- That's how real life works.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.880
That's how medicine works.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.224
I actually just watched the
good doctor COVID-19 episode.

00:09:31.224 --> 00:09:32.750
That's linked down below.
Well worth a watch.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:35.920
Number one, king of medical dramas,

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.560
at least in medical accuracy,
at least in my book,

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:40.463
it is two letters, "ER".

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.170
That's right folks.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:45.020
It's an oldie, but it's
a classic. It's so good.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.760
20, 30 years later since its inception,

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:48.900
it's still bingeable.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:49.970
It's still quality.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.880
It still tells real life
stories about humans.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.790
The issues that we run into hospitals

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:56.900
to this very day still apply

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.780
to the episodes that are found in ER.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.200
It's truly one of my
favorite medical dramas.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.590
The medical accuracy is really solid.

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:04.423
